media: ov7251: use the index of the matched link frequency

The loop looks for a firmware link frequency in the driver's link_freq[] and
leaves its index in j, but link_freq_idx was set from i, the position in the
firmware's list. With a single firmware entry of 319.2 MHz (the Surface's IR
camera) i is 0, so the sensor was set up for and reported 240 MHz.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
@@ -1523,7 +1523,7 @@
 		goto out_free_bus_cfg;
 	}
 
-	ov7251->link_freq_idx = i;
+	ov7251->link_freq_idx = j;
 
 out_free_bus_cfg:
 	v4l2_fwnode_endpoint_free(&bus_cfg);
